<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Stucco repair in Northeast Calgary usually starts with one of four things: hail marks, woodpecker holes, cracks or bulges around windows, or parging flaking at the base of a wall. The City of Calgary groups its neighbourhoods by era, and the northeast runs from 1980s and 1990s areas such as Castleridge, Falconridge and Martindale to 2000s suburbs such as Saddle Ridge, Skyview Ranch and Taradale. That mix means many stucco walls have been through the better part of two decades of Calgary winters.</p><p>Sandstone Stucco Co is advertising paid for by independent Calgary stucco contractors. The site does no repair work itself, holds no trade licence, insurance or warranty, and does not deal with insurers. When you call (403) 555-0148 or email info@sandstonestucco.ca, you are put in touch with an independent contractor, who quotes and contracts directly with you. Start with the <a href='/stucco-repair-calgary/'>stucco repair overview</a> if you want the full picture first.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Northeast Calgary</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Northeast Calgary Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Hail damage scope</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A contractor can look over the wall, photograph the marks and write a repair estimate you can pass to your insurer. Your policy and your insurer decide what is covered, so call your insurer first.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Woodpecker hole repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Northern flicker holes can be patched and reinforced once a hole is empty and nesting is over. The contractor quotes after seeing how many holes there are and how far the damage runs behind the finish.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Cracks, bulges and window perimeters</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Cracks around windows, bulges and soft spots can point to moisture behind the finish. As one Calgary firm puts it, nobody can tell the full extent of water damage until the wall is opened up, so the contractor quotes after seeing it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Foundation parging recoats</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Flaking or patchy parging at the base of the wall can be patched and recoated. Foundation cracks, waterproofing and structural questions are outside a parging quote.</p>
      </div>
</div>
